# The remote desktop (VNC): off by default, a password made up by the OS,
# switched only on the console. The test reaches the OS's port 23, so the
# server runs there; a connection is greeted in the RFB protocol (the full
# protocol is tested in beenet/src/rfb.rs, a viewer on the HP).
@net
@forward
@disk
$ net dhcp
~ ^address 10\.0\.2\.15/24 \(DHCP\)
$ vnc
remote desktop (VNC): off (vnc on [PORT] starts it)
@remote
(no answer)
$ vnc on 23
remote desktop (VNC) on, port 23 (saved)
~ ^password: [a-hjkmnp-z2-9]{8}   \(shown only now; 'vnc password' makes a new one\)$
~ ^not encrypted: the screen and all that is typed can be seen on the network
@remote
RFB 003.008
$ vnc
remote desktop (VNC): on, connect a VNC viewer to 10.0.2.15::23
since boot: 0 logins, 0 wrong passwords; no viewer is connected
$ cat /system/vnc
on 23
$ vnc password
~ ^password: [a-hjkmnp-z2-9]{8}   \(shown only now
# It comes back after a reboot, with the same password.
@reboot
~ \[vnc\]  remote desktop on port 23, not encrypted
$ vnc off
remote desktop (VNC) off (saved)
@remote
(no answer)
$ vnc sideways
usage: vnc [on [PORT] | off | password]
